    {
      "issue": "The sandbox pins that keep temp directories and inherited writable roots out of a Codex worker's write set are emitted only inside the validated linked-worktree branch (after the backlink check passes). A Codex worker whose cwd is a normal checkout, a subdirectory of a linked worktree, or a worktree whose gitdir/backlink validation fails gets no pins, so Codex's default writable roots ($TMPDIR, /tmp, plus any writable_roots from the operator's Codex config) still apply. When the repository's git directory lives under one of those roots, the worker can write common `config`, `hooks/`, and the admin dir's `commondir`/`config.worktree`; the orchestrator's next git command there then runs worker-chosen config (core.fsmonitor, core.hooksPath, core.sshCommand) outside the sandbox. Harmed principal: the operator, via a prompt-injected or misbehaving Codex worker. The README's claim that 'placing a repository in a temp directory does not bypass the boundary' and that forged links 'get no grant' only holds for workers started at a validated linked-worktree root. Unverified against a live Codex (could not run it in this session): the evidence is the launcher code and the branch's own README rationale for the pins. The exposure exists at the base for all of these cases; the branch closes it for one case only.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "471",
      "quote": "      '          set -- \"$@\" -c sandbox_workspace_write.writable_roots=[] -c sandbox_workspace_write.exclude_tmpdir_env_var=true -c sandbox_workspace_write.exclude_slash_tmp=true',",
      "suggestion": "Emit the temp-directory exclusions (exclude_tmpdir_env_var, exclude_slash_tmp) for every Codex worker, or at least whenever `git rev-parse` finds a repository, outside the backlink check; keep only the --add-dir grants conditional on validation. Decide separately whether to clear writable_roots for all workers, since that also drops the pack-installed review-log and field-reports roots. Add a test asserting the pins are present for a normal checkout, a linked-worktree subdirectory and a forged-backlink worktree.",
      "likelihood": 2,
      "impact": 7,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "`acs-agent open sol --cwd <dir>` where <dir> is a normal checkout, a subdirectory of a linked worktree, or a worktree failing the backlink check, and the repository's git directory is under $TMPDIR or /tmp (e.g. a scratch repo created in a temp directory, as the original probe design did). The operator's usual worktrees live in the project folder and are not affected.",
      "preExisting": true,
